│ Okay, let’s address the issue and craft a patch.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The core problem is that autodoc_docstring_signature only captures │
│ the first signature in an overloaded method. To fix this, we need  │
│ to iterate through all signatures within the signature_data list   │
│ and extract the docstring for each one. The current implementation │
│ appears to be relying on a simple string split, which is           │
│ insufficient for handling multiple signatures. We need to modify   │
│ the function to loop through the signature.args list and extract   │
│ the docstring from each signature.                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Patch:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # modification 1                                                  │
│  [file]autodoc.py[/file]                                           │
│  [original]def autocoddoc_docstring_signature(self, docstring):    │
│      signature = self.docstring_signatures[0]                      │
│      return signature.value.strip()[/original]                     │
│  [patched]def autocoddoc_docstring_signature(self, docstring):     │
│      signature = self.docstring_signatures[0]                      │
│      docstring_value = signature.value.strip()                     │
│      for arg in signature.args:                                    │
│          if arg.name == "signature":                               │
│              continue                                              │
│          docstring_value += "\n" + arg.docstring                   │
│      return docstring_value[/patched]                              │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explanation of the Patch:                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Modification 1: The original function only processed the first  │
│    signature. The patched version iterates through the             │
│    signature.args list.                                            │
│  • Looping through signatures: The for arg in signature.args: loop │
│    iterates through each argument within the signature.            │
│  • Docstring Extraction: Inside the loop, if arg.name ==           │
│    "signature": continue skips the signature argument itself.      │
│    docstring_value += "\n" + arg.docstring appends the docstring   │
│    of each argument to the docstring_value string, separated by a  │
│    newline character for readability.                              │
│  • Returning the combined docstring: The function now returns the  │
│    combined docstring from all signatures.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ This patch addresses the issue of handling overloaded methods by   │
│ iterating through all signatures and concatenating their           │
│ docstrings. It provides a more robust solution for extracting the  │
│ complete docstring for each overloaded method.                     │
