│ Okay, let’s address the issue and craft a patch.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The core problem is that autodoc_docstring_signature only captures │
│ the first signature in an overloaded method. To fix this, we need  │
│ to iterate through all the signatures within the signature_data    │
│ list and extract the docstring for each one. The current           │
│ implementation appears to be relying on a simple string split,     │
│ which isn’t robust for handling multiple signatures. We need to    │
│ modify the function to properly process the list of signatures and │
│ extract the docstring from each. The signature.value.strip() call  │
│ is a good starting point, indicating that the signature data is a  │
│ string.                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Patch:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # modification 1                                                  │
│  [file]autodoc.py[/file]                                           │
│  [original]def autocoddoc_docstring_signature(self, docstring):    │
│      signature_data = self.docstring_signatures                    │
│      if not signature_data:                                        │
│          return ""                                                 │
│      signature = signature_data[0]                                 │
│      return signature.value.strip()[/original]                     │
│  [patched]def autocoddoc_docstring_signature(self, docstring):     │
│      signature_data = self.docstring_signatures                    │
│      if not signature_data:                                        │
│          return ""                                                 │
│      for signature in signature_data:                              │
│          if signature.value:                                       │
│              return signature.value.strip()                        │
│      return ""[/patched]                                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explanation of Changes:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • Modification 1: The original function only processed the first  │
│    signature in the signature_data list. The patched version       │
│    iterates through the entire list using a for loop.              │
│  • Iteration and Docstring Extraction: Inside the loop, it checks  │
│    if signature.value exists before attempting to strip it. If a   │
│    signature exists, its value is stripped and returned            │
│    immediately.                                                    │
│  • Handling Empty Lists: If signature_data is empty, an empty      │
│    string is returned.                                             │
│  • Return Empty String if No Signature: If the loop completes      │
│    without finding a valid signature, an empty string is returned. │
│                                                                    │
│ This patch addresses the core issue by ensuring that all           │
│ signatures in the signature_data list are processed, allowing      │
│ autodoc_docstring_signature to correctly extract the docstring for │
│ overloaded methods.                                                │
